---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the Roseville New Church website handles your information, including the analytics we use."
  currentPath="/privacy"
>
  <main class="container-site px-6 md:px-8 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-4">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] prose-rnc">
      <div
        class="font-display font-semibold text-eyebrow tracking-eyebrow uppercase text-accent-primary mb-2.5"
      >
        ✦ Your information
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-0 text-h1">Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        This page explains what this website collects about visitors and how we
        use it. The website is run by The Sydney Society of The New Church
        (Roseville New Church), 2B Shirley Rd, Roseville NSW 2069.
      </p>

      <h2>Website analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to see, in aggregate, how the site is used: which
        pages are visited, roughly where in the world visitors are, what kind of
        device and browser they use, and how they arrived. Google Analytics sets
        cookies on your device to do this. We use the results to improve the
        site, and we do not use them to identify individual visitors.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not run advertising on this site and we do not sell information
        about visitors. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we
        tell Google not to use your visit for advertising. Your visit may still
        be counted in our aggregate figures.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install
        Google's{' '}
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">opt-out browser add-on</a
        >. Google explains how it handles this data in{' '}
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Vercel. Like most hosts, it keeps standard server
        logs (such as your IP address and the pages requested) for security and
        performance.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch and our mailing list</h2>
      <p>
        If you email, phone or write to us, we use the details you give us to
        reply and to look after your enquiry.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you join our mailing list, we ask for your name and email address and
        the lists you want. We first email you a link to confirm, and only then
        add you. We keep your details in Planning Center, our church database,
        and send the confirmation email through Postmark. We use your details to
        send you the news you chose, and every email has an unsubscribe link. You
        can ask us to remove you at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your details, membership and signing in</h2>
      <p>
        When you join the mailing list you can also, if you like, give us your
        title, date of birth, phone number and postal address. Every one of
        these is optional. We keep them in Planning Center with the rest of
        your record, and use them to keep our records right and to post you
        printed items you asked for. Until you confirm your email address, the
        details you entered wait on our server and are deleted automatically
        after 7 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can see and change your details, choose your emails, unsubscribe or
        deactivate your account at any time on our &ldquo;Manage your details&rdquo;
        page. To sign in we email a
        6-digit code to the address we hold for you. The code works once and
        expires after 10 minutes, and a sign-in lasts at most 8 hours (30
        minutes if you stop using the page). We keep short-lived records on our
        server to make this work, such as the code (stored only in scrambled
        form), counts of recent attempts to limit abuse, and a note of which
        details you changed (the names of the fields, never the details
        themselves), which we keep for 2 years. The sign-in cookie is needed for
        the page to work.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you apply to become a member of The Sydney Society of The New Church,
        we record your application, that you affirmed the beliefs the
        Society&rsquo;s constitution asks of members, and the Committee&rsquo;s
        decision. A person&rsquo;s religious belief is sensitive information, so
        we use it only to decide membership and to keep the register of members
        the law requires the Society to keep. Membership records are kept in
        Planning Center, and details of former members are kept for as long as
        the law requires. If you deactivate your account, we stop emailing and
        posting to you but keep a basic record for these reasons. Ask us if you
        would like anything else removed.
      </p>

      <h2>Administrators</h2>
      <p>
        Church administrators sign in to a separate area of this site. Signing
        in uses cookies that are needed for the sign-in to work.
      </p>

      <h2>Other websites</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to other websites and services, such as Facebook,
        Instagram and Zoom. They have their own privacy practices, which we do
        not control.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions, access and changes</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what information we hold about you, or ask us to correct
        or delete it, by emailing{' '}
        <a href="mailto:admin@rosevillenewchurch.com.au"
          >admin@rosevillenewchurch.com.au</a
        >{' '}
        or phoning{' '}
        <a href="tel:+61294167026">02 9416 7026</a>. We may update this page from
        time to time.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated 25 November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
